<title>EGYPT: Egypt buys 30,000T each U.S. corn, soybean - traders.</title>
<headline>Egypt buys 30,000T each U.S. corn, soybean - traders.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt bought on Wednesday 30,000 tonnes of U.S. yellow corn and the same amount of U.S. soybean for delivery in December, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the official Holding Company for Food Industries bought the corn from Swiss-based firm Romak for $131.95 a tonne and the soybean for $276.35 a tonne.</p>
<p>All prices include cost and freight.</p>
<p>-- Miral Fahmy +202 578 3290/91</p>
</text>
